{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu","id":567689,"title":"A Dumb Question - What was in it for the Shan'iatu?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-25T05:08:04-07:00","id":567689,"title":"A Dumb Question - What was in it for the Shan'iatu?","content":"Let me preface this post by saying I've really only skimmed the Corebook but as it specifically states that no-one who undertook the Rite of Return ever arose during the time of Irem... what was the Rite of Return for?<br /> <br /> The Arisen are hugely powerful servants that were never called upon throughout whatever calamity brought the Nameless Empire to an end - this in itself seems unusual. The Rite of Return was supposedly the greatest magic of Irem and yet neither the Empire nor its Sorceror-Priest-Kings seem to have gained any utility from it. What gives?<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that there is an answer in the text or hidden between the lines of the text but my (admittedly cursory reading) has not turned it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T05:35:45-07:00","id":567738,"title":"","content":"Response received via PM that answered this question entirely to my satisfaction.<br /> <br /> Heh-heh-heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocen