refore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T19:52:11-07:00","id":573485,"title":"","content":"Could I also get the PM of Enlightenment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:34:25-07:00","id":574647,"title":"","content":"Waaaaah I wanna be able to talk about Mummy stuff too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T08:22:55-07:00","id":575255,"title":"","content":"Instead of waiting for a PM, why don't we actually talk about the subject?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T09:49:00-07:00","id":575305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=575255#post575255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of waiting for a PM, why don't we actually talk about the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of a weird question, but one that's answered in The Book of the Deceived (albeit by an unreliable narrator). The answer is, spoiler-free: They're hoping that they'll get more where they ended up than where they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T04:34:23-07:00","id":576269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=575255#post575255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of waiting for a PM, why don't we actually talk about the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div> Which subject? Personally, I say with go with Utena myself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T05:52:34-07:00","id":576285,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I wasn't trying to threadcap.<br /> <br /> The explainer indicated that the answer would count as spoilers - and given the strict separation of GM Knowledge from PC Knowledge in the corebook I wanted to respect that.<br /> <br /> I would totally like to see more discussion of the question though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T06:45:45-07:00","id":576308,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm up for participating in speculation from an in-character perspective.<br /> <br /> So, the common guess is &quot;Ascension to godhood&quot;. Perhaps the Shan'iatu became the Judges, or now get to serve the Judges in a more direct manner (sitting at their feet).<br /> <br /> Actually, you know what? I have an idea for a related, but different question: <b><u>What did the<i> Judges</i> get out of the Rite of Return?</u></b> This is good grounds for figuring out if the whole thing was a deception by Ammut, or some more powerful evil godling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T06:27:12-07:00","id":577294,"title":"","content":"Well, I personally think that, somehow, the Shan'iatu and Judges (assuming they're different) have dreams of global domination. They want to build a society that funnels the energy of the living world to them in their &quot;afterlife.&quot; A global theocratic civilization, all with the cults and worshiping. <br /> <br /> I still think that the Judges that were part of the Rite of Return were actually the Shan'iatu after they ascended to godhood. Time gets a little bit wonky when we're talking about beings that exist outside the standard flow of time (which Du'at apparently does). So, that answers what the Judges got out of the Rite - their ascension in the first place!<br /> <br /> I equate the Shan'iatu to the fantasy necromancer lich kings trying to take over the world, and the Arisen as the leaders of the undead hoards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:59:57-07:00","id":577888,"title":"","content":"Tinfoil hat territory.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the shan'iatu were mages from an ancient time who sought to ascend and had harnessed the power of divine fire and made not promthean, but arisen, through the rite of return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T17:22:34-07:00","id":577987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin Engineer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=577888#post577888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tinfoil hat territory.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the shan'iatu were mages from an ancient time who sought to ascend and had harnessed the power of divine fire and made not promthean, but arisen, through the rite of return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not /everything/ needs to be Mages, y'know.<br /> <br /> And Osirans are probably failed attempts at the Rite, not the other way around. There's definitely some sort of funny interaction between Pyros, Sekhem, and pure Supernal goodness, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T19:32:46-07:00","id":578060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=577987#post577987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not /everything/ needs to be Mages, y'know.</div> </div> </div> </div>My rebuttal: <a href=\"http://memegenerator.net/instance2/590788\" target=\"_blank\">http://memegenerator.net/instance2/590788</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Osirans are probably failed attempts at the Rite, not the other way around. </div> </div> </div>I can see that being a likely possibility. Bound to break a few eggs when making an occult omelet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's definitely some sort of funny interaction between Pyros, Sekhem, and pure Supernal goodness, though. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So an osirian promethean and an arisen walk into an bar...<br /> <br /> <br /> (But to be serious about this I do 100% agree that prometheans and arisen are most likely to be cousins of a sort and likely the results of a metaphorical &quot;fork in the road&quot; as they are quiet similar. Osirian prometheans especially as they can keep rebuying the Revivification bestowment each time they die at only Azoth x 5, where they enter a similar effect like a mummy would going through Duat.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6740,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","user":"Goblin Engineer","date":". 07-03-2015, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:15:34-07:00","id":578710,"title":"","content":"My pet theory is that the first osiran was the result of someone trying to make their own mummy, failing, but tapping into the divine fire through their obsession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:47:20-07:00","id":578747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=577987#post577987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not /everything/ needs to be Mages, y'know.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but fairness, ancient sorcerers who pulled off the greatest magical feat the world has ever seen - or maybe the worst, because they broke the world doing it - mages aren't a daft interpretation.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree with Osirians, if linked to mummies, being failed versions of the Rite - more precisely, I think Osirians are a failed shot at the Rite by someone who wanted <i>themselves</i> to be mummy that was made - while the 1st edition Tammuz make more sense as failed versions of the Rite from someone who was looking for servants out of it. (Mekhet have also been brought up as possible Rite-failures).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T12:13:48-07:00","id":579066,"title":"","content":"Why not the other way around? The Shan'iatu, disappointed with humanity, attempted to create better humans, and accidentally came up with a method to make people immortal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T12:44:56-07:00","id":579078,"title":"","content":"One idea I saw floating around from the devs lately is how Kindred clans might have differing origins, even if they're from the same clan. Who's to say Prometheans, who are all created by a near-divine moment, might have different origins despite being similar lineages?<br /> <br /> I'm running on two hours of sleep so I can't really get my words out, but I like Christian A's idea. What I mean, though, is hey it's magic so it's probably a little bit of every theory but mostly something we're not seeing that's behind the in-universe scenes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:26:00-07:00","id":579187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=578747#post578747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but fairness, ancient sorcerers who pulled off the greatest magical feat the world has ever seen - or maybe the worst, because they broke the world doing it - mages aren't a daft interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like pretty much everything in the books implies that the Shan'iatu weren't human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:39:32-07:00","id":579193,"title":"","content":"Deceived more or less flat out states they weren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-05-2015, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:45:35-07:00","id":579196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=579193#post579193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deceived or less flat out states they weren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brace for the part where someone goes &quot;but BotD has an unreliable narrator!&quot; like they always do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:17:49-07:00","id":579333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=579078#post579078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I saw floating around from the devs lately is how Kindred clans might have differing origins, even if they're from the same clan. Who's to say Prometheans, who are all created by a near-divine moment, might have different origins despite being similar lineages?<br /> <br /> I'm running on two hours of sleep so I can't really get my words out, but I like Christian A's idea. What I mean, though, is hey it's magic so it's probably a little bit of every theory but mostly something we're not seeing that's behind the in-universe scenes</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's pretty much canon, since the nuclear prometheans have three separate founders, and the existence of the orphean prometheans within the riven also implies as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T05:59:40-07:00","id":579736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=579196#post579196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brace for the part where someone goes &quot;but BotD has an unreliable narrator!&quot; like they always do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ish... Atlantis and Pangaea stories are told with unreliable narrators, but those two things are required parts of the secret histories of Mage and Wolf.<br /> <br /> So, while the stories aren't always 100% accurate and details can be wrong, the general highlights are not only spot on, but have in game supporting evidence to back it up. And Mummy is rather special among WoD games when it comes to its secret history - its far less flexible than the others.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's the whole animal-headed stuff. For those of us who are still certain that the Shan'iatu are the Judges currently controlling mummies (Death instead of Life), having inhuman Shan'iatu makes more sense than metamorphed humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-05-2015, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:09:17-07:00","id":579742,"title":"","content":"I thought unreliable narrators made up the entity of NWoD metaphysical lore. No one knows anything for sure. Everything can be wrong.<br /> <br /> It was the major difference between CWoD &amp; NWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:49:46-07:00","id":579777,"title":"","content":"In my game the Shan'iatu were, and still are even post-<b>BotD</b>, aliens from another galactic dimension thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:39:11-07:00","id":579812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=579736#post579736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ish... Atlantis and Pangaea stories are told with unreliable narrators, but those two things are required parts of the secret histories of Mage and Wolf.<br /> <br /> So, while the stories aren't always 100% accurate and details can be wrong, the general highlights are not only spot on, but have in game supporting evidence to back it up. And Mummy is rather special among WoD games when it comes to its secret history - its far less flexible than the others.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's the whole animal-headed stuff. For those of us who are still certain that the Shan'iatu are the Judges currently controlling mummies (Death instead of Life), having inhuman Shan'iatu makes more sense than metamorphed humans.</div> </div> </div> </div> The myth of atlantis has a book full of different theories as to what it was, up to and including that it was the hypothetical planet Phaeton.<br /> <br /> Likewise, father wolf and pangea aren't the only origin story werewolves have in the nwod, blasphemies has origins ranging from wolves deciding thumbs would be super cool to have, to celtic demigods, to the devil did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T08:55:54-07:00","id":579866,"title":"","content":"The only thing 'inflexible' for <b>Mummy</b> is the existence of Irem and the Nameless Empire. I think that's fairly light as far as backstory buy-in goes, though it might seem otherwise since the nWoD is just open-ended mythology in the other games.<br /> <br /> I wish there was a bit more information. Upon achieving Apotheosis you're supposed to remember your mortal memories, but we don't know much of what happened then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T10:57:27-07:00","id":579980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=579812#post579812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The myth of atlantis has a book full of different theories as to what it was, up to and including that it was the hypothetical planet Phaeton.<br /> <br /> Likewise, father wolf and pangea aren't the only origin story werewolves have in the nwod, blasphemies has origins ranging from wolves deciding thumbs would be super cool to have, to celtic demigods, to the devil did it.</div> </div> </div> </div> In 2e, they're fact, though. We even had the developers say its a necessary buy in to the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:18:15-07:00","id":579990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=579196#post579196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brace for the part where someone goes &quot;but BotD has an unreliable narrator!&quot; like they always do.</div> </div> </div> </div>My response to this hypothetical person is &quot;Yes, but that only counts so much on certain points when they are speaking of themselves. A unreliable narrator can't possibly be that wrong all the time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T13:16:38-07:00","id":580107,"title":"","content":"I prefer the simplicity of the Shan'iatu being mortal mages (not in the Awakened sense - this is Mummy, not Mage) who thought they found a way to achieve ultimate immortality by tricking an entire empire and creating slaves bound to them for all eternity. <br /> <br /> I don't use much of this in my games - the game is ultimately about the Arisen, not the Shan'iatu and not the Judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T13:22:46-07:00","id":580114,"title":"","content":"Aren't the two / three interrelated? A major part of being a Mummy is that you're the slave of the Judges, and uncovering ancient / secret history. So, isn't it the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T17:09:34-07:00","id":580351,"title":"","content":"Depends on the characters and the game, I think. Some players are going to be hugely invested in their character's history, but are happy to regard the deeper &quot;truths&quot; as vague possibilities that were simply beyond their comprehension in life. Others, particularly if they're playing characters of the Ren decree, might consider revelations of in-universe cosmology as paramount in settling their disposition towards Apotheosis, Arisen orthodoxy, and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:34:43-07:00","id":580456,"title":"","content":"I think the Judges are more necessary in a game than the Shan'iatu, but even then it depends on the themes you're constructing and even then it's if you believe the Shan'iatu are the Judges.<br /> <br /> I don't, though, and I don't think the Shan'iatu are that necessary for the core game. Figuring out how to make them matter was the whole premise behind my longer <b>Mummy</b> game: what happens when an uter relic of one of the actual Shan'iatu is found?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:32:55-07:00","id":580496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=579980#post579980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In 2e, they're fact, though. We even had the developers say its a necessary buy in to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Storytellers determine what's fact and what not in their games, and since OP doesn't have the budget to send ninjas after them, it's going to stay that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:52:14-07:00","id":580505,"title":"","content":"Shan'iatu not being human as far as the books go does not really feel like something that the developer and co would try to unreliable narrator &quot;just cuz.&quot; As far as &quot;CANON&quot; goes as far as the backkstory. I'm more than fine taking it at face value that they were not human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T06:06:50-07:00","id":580853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=580107#post580107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the simplicity of the Shan'iatu being mortal mages (not in the Awakened sense - this is Mummy, not Mage)</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too; my headcanon has them as a thaumaturge/relic-maker mix, maybe with a dash of eternal. In part because I like the idea that rather than simply having scads of power - though they found a huge <i>source</i> of power - what really distinguished them was that they learned to industrialise and engineer their magic in a way no one has since.<br /> <br /> Also in my headcanon is that they were bound to the service of the Judges and wanted out: the Rite was a way of saying here, have these servants instead. (Note that this too is definitely <i>not</i> true in the game canon itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:12:43-07:00","id":581208,"title":"","content":"I disagree with the idea of Shan'iatu as traditional mortals... magic using, or otherwise. The Shan'iatu are obsessively concerned with one single task ; breaking into the afterlife that has been denied them. Again and again they attempt to bust in there, and again and again they get turned away. In fact, the whole reason they start Irem in the first place is one of them gets caught trying to break in again after they murder Azar and Anpu vaguely implies that they ought to try harder at the civilization thing.<br /> <br /> If they were more or less mortal creatures, I don't think they'd have found it so difficult to die like other mortal creatures do. In my opinion they are unique, exceptional creatures.<br /> <br /> Heck, Demons resemble them more, having no 'soul' or afterlife in a similar way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:26:47-07:00","id":581258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=581208#post581208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with the idea of Shan'iatu as traditional mortals... magic using, or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>To reiterate, I wasn't making an interpretation for canon, I was stating a preference for headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:39:28-07:00","id":581550,"title":"","content":"If not human mages, well all those theories surrounding Egypt that involves aliens/eldritch horrors/primordials/gods/etc would be the only other logical step. After all there are plenty of mythologies that talk about &quot;sky people&quot; who made the humans in order to act as a servant-race for their needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:43:48-07:00","id":581629,"title":"","content":"Or, you know, we can agree on the entire fallen divine entities theory that <i>the game itself is telling us they were</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not that hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T03:41:26-07:00","id":583318,"title":"","content":"My rough draft backstory involves the Shan'iatu being mortal occultists in a very low weirdness setting who pretty much stumble ass backwards into a right-place-right-time situation where they bridge a small gap in the dimensions and gain a sponsor; later in their hubris they push things too far and open up the whole world to a slew of supernatural horror. Cue their empire constantly fighting things like the Strix or Inferno demons. Oops. <br /> <br /> I'm aware that this doesn't mesh up with BotDeceived at all. To be honest, I'm considering axing the whole idea of the Shadow for this particular cosmology, and I care far more for that than I do a random story in BotDeceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T06:16:10-07:00","id":583424,"title":"","content":"Going back to the Shan'iatu/mage thing for a moment, the objection based on Book of the Deceived is that the first chapter's narrator says that the Shan'iatu weren't human, and predated humans too (though they were made in the image of what humans would be, rather than humans being made in theirs) - and yes, whatever the reliability of that narrator, we pretty much have to take that as canon.<br /> <br /> But even so, their abilities and ambitions still have many parallels, and if you did want to link them, you could do it on the basis not that the Shan'iatu were human, but that mages - though they have forgotten it - aren't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:21:15-07:00","id":583568,"title":"","content":"I'm just glad the developer and writers would not be rude enough to make them mages. It would be against the intended magical niche that was chosen for Mummy and would be nothing but disingenuous to Mummy fans and not a favour to Mage fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T14:05:15-07:00","id":583828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even so, their abilities and ambitions still have many parallels, and if you did want to link them, you could do it on the basis not that the Shan'iatu were human, but that mages - though they have forgotten it - aren't. </div> </div> </div>You got there before I could; that seems like the much more interesting reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just glad the developer and writers would not be rude enough to make them mages. It would be against the intended magical niche that was chosen for Mummy and would be nothing but disingenuous to Mummy fans and not a favour to Mage fans. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting use of 'rude'. If it'd been intended, the whole work would have changed to reflect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:51:21-07:00","id":583944,"title":"","content":"Seeing as how no game is so blatantly crossover'd, except <b>Beast</b> (which still stands on its own), I don't see how it'd be even an option to integrate <b>Mage</b> so much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T20:49:09-07:00","id":584117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=583568#post583568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just glad the developer and writers would not be rude enough to make them mages. It would be against the intended magical niche that was chosen for Mummy and would be nothing but disingenuous to Mummy fans and not a favour to Mage fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>True be told, all the game lines (with the exception of Beast) tend to live in their own little world at times and Mummy seems to ramps this up to 11.<br /> <br /> That being said, I could easily see the Shan'iatu starting off as something old and otherworldly only to *cough* descend into merely being demigods. Also have really no issue with mortal sorcerers running around with access to Sekhem who aren't the Awakened.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is a big place and not even the Kindred hold a monopoly on 'Vampire' in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:44:22-07:00","id":584836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=583944#post583944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as how no game is so blatantly crossover'd, except <b>Beast</b> (which still stands on its own), I don't see how it'd be even an option to integrate <b>Mage</b> so much</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's an option; why wouldn't it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:32:08-07:00","id":584864,"title":"","content":"Because every game line (except <b>Beast</b>, which as I said could still stand alone) has a pretty strict policy of not using the setting metaphysics of other game lines to explain its own?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't in your own games, but why would the writers say they're capital M Mages in a <b>Mummy</b> book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:43:07-07:00","id":584871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=584864#post584864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying you can't in your own games, but why would the writers say they're capital M Mages in a <b>Mummy</b> book?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is saying they would.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T18:53:14-07:00","id":585517,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what TyrannicalRabbit was talking about then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T22:49:37-07:00","id":585674,"title":"","content":"On top of the Book of the Deceived, the Hellenistic Mage chapter for Dark Eras does everything but flat-out say that the Shan'iatu weren't Awakened Mages. Sekhem is not really connected with the Supernal Realms (or at least not any more than, say, rocks or trees are), and Egyptian Mages in later eras are aware of it but are not very good at manipulating it.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to believe that the mythic history of the Shan'iatu as presented in BotD is mostly true in broad strokes; any or all of the specific details may be fabricated or altered, but the &quot;fallen divine entities&quot; angle is as good as any other. After all, no one else has ever managed to reproduce the Rite of Return (though the Purified are conspicuously similar in some ways), and one would assume that later generations of mortal thaumaturges had many advantages over the Shan'iatu in terms of opportunities for study and past discoveries to build upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-10-2015, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T08:16:48-07:00","id":648975,"title":"","content":"I like Unified Continuity Theories, so in my games, the Shan'iatu are refugees (or the children of refugees) from Atlantis' collapse, originally occupying the Free Council's place in the Pentacle. They were desperate to shore up their failing connection to the Supernal. They turned to all sorts of strange practices, eventually contacting the Judges and learning how to manipulate Sekhem. They created the mummies as pale reflections of their ancient servants in Atlantis. The Nameless Empire's end was brought about by the remaining Atlantean mages purging them for turning too far from the path of Wisdom, or by the Seers of the Throne for not turning far enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:46:03-07:00","id":649196,"title":"","content":"Again, Book of the Deceived more or less makes it canon that they're fallen(congealed, more like) divine entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T13:35:21-07:00","id":649271,"title":"","content":"And in terms of unified continuity, they match up better with Marco Singe's stories about the God-Machine's Second Children anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:49:57-07:00","id":649339,"title":"","content":"Yes, because Marco Singe isn't insane.<br /> <br /> Remind me what God Machine Demons are again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:02:46-07:00","id":649346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=649339#post649339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because Marco Singe isn't insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as we've had a point made about ableism concerning mental illness in the last month and &quot;The God-Machine <i>lies all the time</i>&quot; is a textual aspect of Descent, I have to highlight the fact that this is a bad argument to use for the general point of &quot;Marco Singe is inherently unreliable as a source of directly truthful information about the World of Darkness.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remind me what God Machine Demons are again? </div> </div> </div>Yet another set of material beings that messes with fate, causality, culture, et. al.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:36:13-07:00","id":649373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=649339#post649339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because Marco Singe isn't insane.<br /> <br /> Remind me what God Machine Demons are again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Marco Singe isn't reliable. Which is <i>precisely</i> why I hardly believe him when he says that the Animal-Headed Demigods who ruled pre-dynastic Egypt were in any way, shape, or form God-Machine Demons.<br /> <br /> Not that I usually care one whit about crossing game lines, but of all the possibilities that's the one that appeals to me the most. Particularly since it essentially boils down to &quot;the Shan'iatu are exactly what Book of the Deceived says they are, but Marco Singe just assigns them to the wrong cosmic entity.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:40:14-07:00","id":649391,"title":"","content":"@ Satchel: I've missed the ableism argument, and admit that's not fair given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> But still, the point is that the myth he establishes in Voice of an Angel about the Second Children is somewhat undermined by Descent's existence. We know that Demons are not elevated animals. Might they be an example of how the God-machine perceives or twists the image of the Shan'iatu and their servants? Sure, I might concede that, but that's not indicative of much-I sincerely doubt the Deceived(who are the only ones we can confirm have contact with the Shan'iatu right now) know about the Crypt of the Butterfly, as an example.<br /> <br /> I admit bias. Part of it is just how tired I am of people trying to explain the Children of the Temakh as something else from other games in the World, particularly the God-Machine and mages. Given how insular Mummy is with it's lore and design, I find it really grating for people to do this. It goes double since so much of what we're told in Deceived(yes, I see the irony) builds on it's own fundamental suggestion about what the Shan'iatu are, and how well it ties into everything else in Mummy. So much of the narrative is wrapped up in the identity of the Shan'iatu as established that a whole metric crap-ton falls apart when you stick in something else.<br /> <br /> Course, the larger part of it is just that I disdain &quot;all the game lines tie together&quot; as a theory anyways, and yes, this is coming from a guy who really likes Beast.<br /> <br /> @Azahul: I can get behind Marco having the wrong idea, so long as we keep in mind that he has the wrong idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-02-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:49:31-07:00","id":649424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=649391#post649391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Course, the larger part of it is just that I disdain &quot;all the game lines tie together&quot; as a theory anyways, and yes, this is coming from a guy who really likes Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I 100% agree with this. I don't even particularly like crossover, let alone overarching meta-theories on the interconnectivity of game-lines. Just so we're clear. I don't honestly believe that any part of Mummy's cosmology is dredged from the depths of another game line.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're going to insist on doing it, I find it odd that you'd go for Mage for your tie-in (because, what, the Shan'iatu were humanish and used magic?) when Voice of an Angel is sitting there actually talking about the time period and beings who sound a hell of a lot like Shan'iatu (physically, at least).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=649391#post649391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've missed the ableism argument, and admit that's not fair given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> But still, the point is that the myth he establishes in Voice of an Angel about the Second Children is somewhat undermined by Descent's existence. We know that Demons are not elevated animals. Might they be an example of how the God-machine perceives or twists the image of the Shan'iatu and their servants? Sure, I might concede that, but that's not indicative of much-I sincerely doubt the Deceived(who are the only ones we can confirm have contact with the Shan'iatu right now) know about the Crypt of the Butterfly, as an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;An example of how the God-Machine perceives or twists the image of the Shan'iatu&quot; was precisely what I was getting at, yeah.<br /> <br /> That said, of any non-God-Machine related splat, I do think the Deceived are one of the most likely to know about the Crypt of the Butterfly. They're habitually looking in the right direction, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:27:34-07:00","id":649512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/567689-a-dumb-question-what-was-in-it-for-the-shan-iatu?p=649391#post649391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit bias. Part of it is just how tired I am of people trying to explain the Children of the Temakh as something else from other games in the World, particularly the God-Machine and mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The frequency with which you've kicked off that particular jerk of the knee lately renders me wholly unsympathetic to this specific instance, even setting aside the explicit dev-and-writer commentary to the effect that Mummy's metaphysical actors are not &quot;actually&quot; things from parts of the World of Darkness established elsewhere that should obviate the need to do more than cite those statements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given how insular Mummy is with it's lore and design, I find it really grating for people to do this. It goes double since so much of what we're told in Deceived(yes, I see the irony) builds on it's own fundamental suggestion about what the Shan'iatu are, and how well it ties into everything else in Mummy. So much of the narrative is wrapped up in the identity of the Shan'iatu as established that a whole metric crap-ton falls apart when you stick in something else. </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, if I were to suggest the God-Machine has anything to do with any part of Mummy's content, it's a vague association with a one-off tidbit in <i>Sothis Ascends</i> through similarities cutting into the esoterica of a completely separate game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:28:50-07:00","id":649513,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}